---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="How PerkCommons works" description="How PerkCommons researches, reviews, publishes, and maintains open opportunity data.">
  <section class="container py-14">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand">How it works</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-semibold">A public index with a visible editorial trail.</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted">PerkCommons makes credible opportunities easier to discover while keeping the data portable, reviewable, and free.</p>

    <ol class="mt-14 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-line bg-line md:grid-cols-5">
      {["Submit", "Screen", "Research", "Review", "Maintain"].map((step, index) => <li class="bg-surface p-5"><span class="text-xs font-semibold text-brand">0{index + 1}</span><p class="mt-3 font-semibold">{step}</p></li>)}
    </ol>

    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-2">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What source research means</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Automated research may fetch provider pages, record evidence metadata, and suggest a provisional availability state. Automated research is labeled as such and remains pending human review; it cannot create a human-review event by itself.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What human review means</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">A moderator checks the provider evidence and the material claims recorded on a listing. Human-reviewed records carry explicit review provenance, checked claims, and a real review timestamp. A source check is not a guarantee of acceptance, provider conduct, future availability, safety, or outcome.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What “Verified” means</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Verified is narrower than “schema v2” or “source checked.” It is shown only when a record has completed human review and the structured evidence, checked claims, current status, geography, and freshness fields required by the publication rules are present.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What belongs here</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Default discovery prioritizes selective, restricted, time-limited, materially valuable, or difficult-to-discover opportunities. Ordinary free products, public datasets, communities, and general memberships are classified as resources and should not crowd out opportunities.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Corrections and removals</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Anyone may report a broken link, expiry, incorrect claim, duplicate, scam concern, or privacy issue. Reports do not remove records automatically. A moderator records a decision; urgent tombstones can suppress a route while a validated Git change and static rebuild repair the public dataset.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">Disputed, sensitive, sponsor-related, and appealed decisions can require an independent second reviewer in the moderation workflow.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Editorial independence</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Payment never purchases factual approval, verification, or removal of a competitor. Sponsored placements require an explicit public disclosure and remain subject to the same evidence rules.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Privacy boundaries</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Published factual records and their Git history are public. Contributor contact details, reporter details, private notes, assignments, and moderation research stay in the private workflow. Queue summaries deliberately omit private submission bodies and identities.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Known data limitations</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Legacy records and records still awaiting human review may lack complete structured provenance, deadlines, application links, or geography. PerkCommons publishes those gaps in its quality reporting instead of presenting missing evidence as verified fact.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-line pt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Accountability</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-muted">PerkCommons is currently operated by Nataniel Bogacki. Moderation decisions, publication changes, and public data history are designed to leave an auditable trail. Governance and policy work remains public and may evolve as the project grows.</p>
      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm font-medium">
        <a href="/trust/">Trust and transparency</a>
        <a href="/data-quality/">Data quality</a>
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy notice</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/CodWasTaken/docs">Project policies</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/PerkCommons/data/issues">Propose a correction</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/PerkCommons/site">Inspect the source</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>